# local/extio.tcl -- rig-local extio configuration
#
# Sourced at the END of config/extioconf.tcl, after discovery and wiring are
# set up, so anything declared here wins over db-persisted values at boot.
# Absent file = all defaults. An error in this file aborts only the extio
# subprocess's config (see local/README for what that costs and how to spot it).

# ---- obs-leader auto-bind consent ------------------------------------------
# Opt this rig into auto-binding the ESS obs scheduler to a box that announces
# itself as obs leader (box side: config/obs/mode leader + config/obs/pin <n>
# + cmd/save on the box console).
#
# The value is a NAME FILTER, *not* a boolean:
#   off          never auto-bind (the default)
#   auto         bind whatever single box announces obs_leader
#   <boxname>    bind only that box (e.g. box01)
#
# The line below is this rig's DECLARED setting: it re-asserts at every dserv
# boot. A runtime `send extio {extio_obs_autobind auto}` still works (and
# persists to settings.db), but the next boot re-asserts this file's value --
# edit here for anything meant to outlive a restart. To turn auto-bind off,
# declare `off` explicitly rather than deleting the line: a deleted line falls
# back to whatever settings.db last persisted, which may surprise you.
#
# extio_obs_autobind auto

# ---- other rig-local extio overrides ---------------------------------------
# Port pinning, extra forwards, etc. This file runs inside the extio
# subprocess interp with all of extioconf.tcl's procs available.
